From c1b47f2d6e26bb1bee55c90c88be95ccb61c3f31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fritchii Intel fixes <intel-fixes@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:11:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] vulkan_device: "Automatic" movie upscaler stays on the
 bilinear copy on Intel's 8x16x16 path

With cooperative matrices on, g_native_tensor_ops made "Automatic" run the game's own movie
network (32-lane tensor programs f9ea14a22394f5b1, eff3ccbe1438679d, ...). On Intel's 8x16x16
path it drew a pink line and speckled columns over OoT's title movie. Gameplay HMMA programs keep
the matrices.

Tested: Arc B580, title screen screenshots at fixed frame counts are clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_device.cpp | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_device.cpp b/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_device.cpp
index 76030535d..c8688158a 100644
--- a/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_device.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_device.cpp
@@ -1904,8 +1904,12 @@ void Device::RemoveUnsuitableExtensions() {
                                            features.cooperative_matrix,
                                            VK_KHR_COOPERATIVE_MATRIX_EXTENSION_NAME);
     }
-    VideoCommon::Nx2Perf::g_native_tensor_ops.store(extensions.cooperative_matrix,
-                                                    std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    // Picks the movie upscaler (Automatic: the game's own network where tensor operations are
+    // native). Not on Intel's 8x16x16 path: OoT's movie network (its 32-lane compute programs,
+    // f9ea14a22394f5b1 and others) drew a pink line and speckled columns over the title movie on
+    // an Arc B580, the bilinear copy does not. The gameplay HMMA programs keep the matrices.
+    VideoCommon::Nx2Perf::g_native_tensor_ops.store(
+        extensions.cooperative_matrix && !cooperative_hmma_8x16x16, std::memory_order_relaxed);
 
     // VK_KHR_workgroup_memory_explicit_layout
     extensions.workgroup_memory_explicit_layout =
-- 
